<block><txt break.before="1">An Act to refer certain matters relating to
corporations and financial products and services to the Parliament of the
Commonwealth for the purposes of section 51 (xxxvii) of the <legref
jurisd="CTH" type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="no">Constitution of
the Commonwealth</name></legref>.</txt></block></tier>
</content>


<content type="body">

<level type="clause" id="sec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_90ad29c6-4b55-4242-8883-8ebefc1d1a85"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>1</no><heading guid="_a921b1d4-0c3e-4fdb-9ac2-7fcbc9f1573c"
id="sec.1-he"><b>Name and purpose of Act</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.1-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_686204e9-5272-4a44-9df9-0bd4d07fe5af"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.1-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act is the <legref jurisd="NSW" type="act"
check="unknown" refid="act-2001-001"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Corporations
(Commonwealth Powers) Act 2001</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.1-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_6b5a8487-6ee9-4bef-9bf5-07702acbaea8"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.1-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The purpose of this Act is to refer certain
matters relating to corporations and financial products and services to the
Parliament of the Commonwealth for the purposes of section 51 (xxxvii) of the
<legref jurisd="CTH" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="no">Constitution of the Commonwealth</name></legref>, so as to
enable that Parliament to make laws that apply of their own force in the
State, instead of those matters being dealt with by the <legref jurisd="NSW"
type="act" check="unknown" refid="sl-1999-0703"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Corporations Law</i></name></legref> and other applied
laws.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.1-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_1c9194b4-d980-4d18-860c-e965d49d80bb"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.1-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Nothing in this Act is intended to enable the
making of a law pursuant to the amendment reference with the sole or main
underlying purpose or object of regulating industrial relations matters even
if, but for this subsection, the law would be a law with respect to a matter
referred to the Parliament of the Commonwealth by the amendment
reference.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_8af3f668-4897-431a-ae76-369953a70ff8"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>2</no><heading guid="_e3bed2a3-0eb6-4438-9836-a5d21475fca6"
id="sec.2-he"><b>Commencement</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act commences on a day or days to be
appointed by proclamation.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
