<head>
<no>3</no><heading guid="_32bf0bf4-91c2-40cc-95d2-34de3231fcd5"
id="sec.3-he"><b>Definitions</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_f0d6975f-401d-4f62-b8d2-eed8e67bace1"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Act:</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_67004c56-c384-4bee-a176-f8038499f485"
id="sec.3-def.amendmentreference"><b><i>amendment reference</i></b></defterm>
means the reference under section 4 (1) (b).</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_53037240-aabe-4437-875e-b770962e506c"
id="sec.3-def.commencementday"><b><i>commencement day</i></b></defterm> means
the day on which section 4 (1) commences.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_ed238c97-4863-4b02-b421-ec87930087db"
id="sec.3-def.Corporationsinstrument"><b><i>Corporations
instrument</i></b></defterm> means any instrument made or issued under the
Corporations legislation.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_804f535a-1546-4c4b-b186-f97bf8f0b3a1"
id="sec.3-def.Corporationslegislation"><b><i>Corporations
legislation</i></b></defterm> means Commonwealth Acts enacted in the terms, or
substantially in the terms, of the tabled text and as in force from time to
time.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_584459e7-2992-4187-8bd0-aa91087985be"
id="sec.3-def.expressamendment"><b><i>express amendment</i></b></defterm> of
the Corporations legislation means the direct amendment of the text of the
Corporations legislation (whether by the insertion, omission, repeal,
substitution or relocation of words or matter) by Commonwealth Acts, but does
not include the enactment by a Commonwealth Act of a provision that has or
will have substantive effect otherwise than as part of the text of the
Corporations legislation.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_f432188e-0713-43f3-9a01-1587692199ca"
id="sec.3-def.initialreference"><b><i>initial reference</i></b></defterm>
means the reference under section 4 (1) (a).</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_437655c9-98ad-4730-bd8e-b5a9e92c138c"
id="sec.3-def.prescribedterminationday"><b><i>prescribed termination
day</i></b></defterm> means the day on which both the references are to
terminate as set out in section 5 (1).</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_2d30538f-ea29-4a4d-b0d1-4122b1c8e0a9"
id="sec.3-def.reference"><b><i>reference</i></b></defterm> means:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_8eeca700-2844-49c7-81fb-e54e899b1f8c" id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the initial reference, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_f0eca9bd-9b1c-421a-980a-dcff4c201cea" id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the amendment
reference.</txt></block></li></list>
</block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_2bb8b68f-7854-4a64-98f7-cddacde55933"
id="sec.3-def.referredprovisions"><b><i>referred provisions</i></b></defterm>
means the tabled text to the extent to which that text deals with matters that
are included in the legislative powers of the Parliament of the
State.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_e91ca212-7c19-4493-8343-101e705ec3fe"
id="sec.3-def.tabledtext"><b><i>tabled text</i></b></defterm> means the text
of the following proposed Bills for Commonwealth Acts, comprised in two or
more documents (each bearing identification as &#8220;part of the tabled
text&#8221;) as tabled by or on behalf of the Attorney General in the
Legislative Assembly at any time during the period between the giving of
notice of motion for leave to introduce the Bill for this Act in the
Legislative Assembly and the second reading of that Bill in the Legislative
Assembly:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_1899aecb-70a8-43e6-a20f-dba9314a3c4d" id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.a-oc.2">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1"><legref jurisd="CTH" type="bill"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Corporations Bill
2001</i></name></legref>,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_d43e7c87-1fd6-47af-94a8-c1bb88bf03d2" id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.b-oc.2">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1"><legref jurisd="CTH" type="bill"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Australian Securities and Investments
Commission Bill 2001</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></deflist>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_faff8a4f-1bd4-44d3-8144-30bcd5f59906"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">If a proclamation terminating the amendment
reference alone has been published under section 7 and has not been revoked,
the expression <defterm type="definition"
guid="_67a301b3-f45b-4522-a9d3-54e8b8ab3abd"
id="sec.3-def.thereferences"><b><i>the references</i></b></defterm> refers to
the initial reference only.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_1e8c388c-663b-4afd-b85b-583b56cd4d68"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>4</no><heading guid="_1f08d345-0e14-4eab-94f5-944fd2db7545"
id="sec.4-he"><b>Reference of matters</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_9979b9df-1e3d-47ef-82b2-547b15e4b136"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The following matters are referred to the
Parliament of the Commonwealth:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_dd73feb8-1db9-4e8f-a496-14d14f8c8e12" id="sec.4-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the matters to which the referred provisions
relate, but only to the extent of the making of laws with respect to those
matters by including the referred provisions in Acts enacted in the terms, or
substantially in the terms, of the tabled text (including laws containing
provisions that authorise the making of Corporations instruments that affect
the operation of the Corporations legislation, otherwise than by express
amendment), and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_e1226078-00d6-4736-9e52-7a35f998c25e" id="sec.4-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the matters of the formation of corporations,
corporate regulation and the regulation of financial products and services,
but only to the extent of the making of laws with respect to those matters by
making express amendments of the Corporations legislation (including laws
inserting or amending provisions that authorise the making of Corporations
instruments that affect the operation of the Corporations legislation,
otherwise than by express amendment).</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_c0e0c4c7-4391-4cb0-bf1f-ba64d6d91f52"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The reference of a matter under subsection (1)
has effect only:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_329cc518-ac54-4499-9891-4b47a5afbb8b" id="sec.4-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">if and to the extent that the matter is not
included in the legislative powers of the Parliament of the Commonwealth
(otherwise than by a reference under section 51 (xxxvii) of the <legref
jurisd="CTH" type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="no">Constitution of
the Commonwealth</name></legref>), and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_6d43101c-6505-42bf-b3fb-cef3bd7194b1" id="sec.4-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">if and to the extent that the matter is included
in the legislative powers of the Parliament of the
State.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_45934e9e-119b-4384-93c8-e79155612f40"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The operation of each paragraph of subsection (1)
is not affected by the other paragraph.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_770e6960-b8dc-45fb-bc60-868ca835f636"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">For the avoidance of doubt, it is the intention
of the Parliament of the State that:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_97a85751-daf5-4173-b886-40da9a8b14a9" id="sec.4-ssec.4-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the Corporations legislation may be expressly
amended, or have its operation otherwise affected, at any time on or after the
commencement day by provisions of Commonwealth Acts the operation of which is
based on legislative powers that the Parliament of the Commonwealth has apart
from the references, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_3202d077-98e0-4f23-a70c-2952f306a204" id="sec.4-ssec.4-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the Corporations legislation may have its
operation affected, otherwise than by express amendment, at any time on or
after the commencement day by provisions of Corporations instruments,
and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_9e76369a-8a73-4d55-b60e-a5effecc4f5b" id="sec.4-ssec.4-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the references are not made subject to any
condition relating to:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_1cda451f-f5db-4d0f-a729-29b8b4da2f66"
id="sec.4-ssec.4-para1.c-para2.i">
<no>(i)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the express amendment or affecting of the
Corporations legislation by provisions referred to in paragraph (a),
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_c64e53c8-7cb0-448a-931e-1ad8dd41632c"
id="sec.4-ssec.4-para1.c-para2.ii">
<no>(ii)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the affecting of the Corporations legislation by
provisions referred to in paragraph (b).</txt></block></li></list>
</block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_b1e82988-68da-4af7-8156-9c1d0a6cc3a9"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(5)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Despite any other provision of this section, a
reference has effect for a period:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_361393a3-219d-4f9d-8bc2-10b4eedc965c" id="sec.4-ssec.5-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">beginning at the beginning of the commencement
day, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_9028176e-f941-4da2-ae95-6c0e3cca7bff" id="sec.4-ssec.5-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">ending at the beginning of the day on which it
terminates as set out in section 5,</txt></block></li></list>

<txt break.before="1">but not longer.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_59642c5f-03c5-4ec6-942e-5a07769149dc"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>5</no><heading guid="_e0751ac7-260a-49d9-be7e-efdcccf276e2"
id="sec.5-he"><b>Termination of references</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_13339047-42fc-4fbb-8713-b8c72a089e79"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Subject to earlier termination under this
section, the references terminate on the day that is the fifth anniversary of
the day of commencement of the Corporations legislation or on a later day
fixed by the Governor by proclamation under section 6.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_4558af95-b1c6-45ca-ad1a-aed63442ee50"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Both the references terminate on a day that is
earlier than the prescribed termination day if the Governor fixes that earlier
day by proclamation under section 7 as the day on which the references
terminate.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_c790e84d-101c-4447-9039-5fd974d1c798"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The amendment reference alone terminates on a day
that is earlier than the prescribed termination day if the Governor fixes that
earlier day by proclamation under section 7 as the day on which the amendment
reference terminates.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_027e6f5e-615d-4339-aaf1-1e9b3b7f7d0e"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">If the amendment reference terminates before the
initial reference, the termination of the amendment reference does not
affect:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_2e3623b0-de15-4f23-810f-aaab34306e11" id="sec.5-ssec.4-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">laws that were made under the amendment reference
before that termination but have not come into operation before that
termination, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_e2283faf-f115-46b9-a5eb-53a74c9c46a4" id="sec.5-ssec.4-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the continued operation in the State of the
Corporations legislation as in operation immediately before that termination
or as subsequently amended or affected by:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_61d5cb13-4b19-4b76-a0f7-c1bed71fa273"
id="sec.5-ssec.4-para1.b-para2.i">
<no>(i)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">laws referred to in paragraph (a),
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_a916a768-e283-45b5-ae2b-b147e8883d53"
id="sec.5-ssec.4-para1.b-para2.ii">
<no>(ii)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">provisions referred to in section 4 (4) (a) or
(b).</txt></block></li></list>
</block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_31cd734a-39da-4fa4-9801-e0f4cc1813ca"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(5)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">For the purposes of subsection (4):</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_1a11334f-bfda-400d-8d8b-118c93c2ca76" id="sec.5-ssec.5-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the laws referred to in subsection (4) (a)
include Corporations instruments, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_dde35d8b-7fc2-4611-91b8-6311f749da7c" id="sec.5-ssec.5-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the reference in subsection (4) (b) to the
Corporations legislation as in operation immediately before the termination of
the amendment reference includes that legislation as affected by Corporations
instruments that have come into operation before that
time.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.6">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_be7b9ada-05d4-42b4-b3a4-cd6571537f19"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>6</no><heading guid="_f03c992f-5421-4240-9c1a-f5c3f541b901"
id="sec.6-he"><b>Extension of period of reference by
proclamation</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_3ebbdb15-4377-4b92-bd1d-8f364448c017"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor may, at any time before the
prescribed termination day, by proclamation published on the NSW legislation
website, fix a day that is later than the prescribed termination day as the
day on which both the references terminate.</txt></block>
<note type="editorial" guid="_a04231a5-c9bd-4e9f-8513-b539f4c9d37b"
id="sec.6-ssec.1-note"><heading guid="_35f96924-68bd-4e32-9a96-c8bcf681830b"
id="sec.6-ssec.1-note-he"><b>Editorial note&#8212;</b></heading>
<block><txt break.before="1">For proclamations pursuant to this subsection,
see Gazette No 82 of 23.6.2006, p 4565; 2011 (128) LW 3.3.2011; 2016 (319) LW
10.6.2016 and 2021 (358) LW 2.7.2021.</txt></block></note>
</tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_5f0fea8f-16b7-47dd-84a0-d6b338e25487"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">More than one proclamation may be made under
subsection (1).</txt></block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 6:</b> Am 2009 No 106,
Sch 3.13.</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.7">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_546b638b-536f-4864-8e67-d45d2646ce0c"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>7</no><heading guid="_7b4955c3-de67-41e3-afa3-5e6ffa98a386"
id="sec.7-he"><b>Earlier termination of reference by
proclamation</b></heading></head>

<pre type="auto-inserted">

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_f4d95968-ad29-4d83-81c0-15fedccb86f4"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor may, at any time, by proclamation
published on the NSW legislation website, fix a day that is earlier than the
prescribed termination day as the day on which:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_8f78024b-3da3-43d8-8f2b-1abbfc97285c" id="sec.7-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the references terminate, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_9b72c57b-52eb-4b78-be4b-aade9f496009" id="sec.7-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the amendment reference
terminates.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_fdb853df-c819-437f-a547-deaeb104734e"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The day fixed under subsection (1) must be no
earlier than the first day after the end of the period of 6 months beginning
with the day on which the proclamation is published under that
subsection.</txt></block></tier>
</pre>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_507147ce-b738-4c3f-ac76-3799328ea08b"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor may, by proclamation published on
the NSW legislation website, revoke a proclamation published under subsection
(1), in which case the revoked proclamation is taken (for the purposes of
section 5) never to have been published.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_638ec3bf-76f0-4f8b-a023-ed24d7a49ff5"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A revoking proclamation has effect only if
published before the day fixed under subsection (1).</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_68d72b5f-e4d5-4079-b78a-9ecd81458df0"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(5)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The revocation of a proclamation published under
subsection (1) does not prevent publication of a further proclamation under
that subsection.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.6">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_8b337657-2508-4cc4-9ed6-92a44fdb86e2"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.6"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(6)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A proclamation under subsection (1) has effect
despite any earlier proclamation published under section 6
(1).</txt></block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 7:</b> Am 2009 No 106,
Sch 3.13.</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.8">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_09d6b97d-3bd9-4cea-bb00-b91762fd9a35"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>8</no><heading guid="_77134df4-7f6a-474e-9318-fa883f6665f7"
id="sec.8-he"><b>Evidence</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.8-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_5e0fac6c-43ba-4653-91b5-ad88169098fd"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A certificate of the Clerk of the Legislative
Assembly of New South Wales certifying that a document is an accurate copy of
the tabled text, or is an accurate copy of a particular part or of particular
provisions of the tabled text, is admissible in evidence in any proceedings
and is evidence:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_04a3f4ed-3601-492e-b5cb-82066581ab67" id="sec.8-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">of the matter certified, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_823f4045-49d3-4c38-bdce-dbbbdfc253d5" id="sec.8-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">that the text of proposed Commonwealth Bills was
tabled in the Legislative Assembly of New South Wales as referred to in the
definition of <defterm type="definition"
guid="_7cecd407-1d7d-4970-9565-7f54ca394713"
id="sec.8-ssec.1-def.tabledtext"><b><i>tabled text</i></b></defterm> in
section 3.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.8-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_a9a4b20b-610c-447b-b479-47363df2f558"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Subsection (1) does not affect any other way in
which the tabling or content of the tabled text, or the accuracy of a copy of
the tabled text or of a part or provisions of the tabled text, may be
established.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.9">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_539817d0-3131-4475-936d-3375754bf840"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.9"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>9</no><heading guid="_e435a069-829f-4b82-9a57-c043e82f248a"
id="sec.9-he"><b>Operation of Act</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act has effect despite any provision of the
<legref jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown" refid="act-1990-083"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Corporations (New South Wales) Act 1990</i></name></legref>
or of the applicable provisions (as defined in that Act) of the
State.</txt></block></level>
</content>


